  "caption": "Quinn borrowed a walking stick for a sore right knee and held it on the same side, set ski-pole tall.\n\nA stick usually works best in the hand opposite the sore leg. That gives leverage that takes over some of the hip muscles' work.\n\nWhat often helps: moving the stick together with the sore leg, setting the handle at wrist-crease height with a slight elbow bend, going up stairs with the good leg first and down with the sore leg and stick, using the rail, and replacing worn tips and grips. If balance is a real problem, a wheeled frame may suit better.\n\nA leg giving way, new numbness or weakness, a sudden decline, or a fall with a head knock needs prompt assessment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
